          "text": "# AI SDK 6 Beta: Breaking Changes & Migration Guide\n\n## Overview\nAI SDK 6 introduces the v3 Language Model Specification with minimal breaking changes compared to AI SDK 5. The version bump reflects specification improvements rather than complete redesign.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\nnpm install ai@beta @ai-sdk/openai@beta @ai-sdk/react@beta\n```\n\n**Note:** Pin to specific versions during beta, as breaking changes may occur in patch releases.\n\n## Key New Features\n\n### 1. **Agent Abstraction**\n- New unified `Agent` interface for building agents with full execution control\n- Default `ToolLoopAgent` implementation handles tool execution loops automatically\n- Supports custom agent implementations via interface extension\n\n### 2. **Tool Execution Approval**\n- Set `needsApproval: true` on tools to require user confirmation before execution\n- Dynamic approval using conditional logic based on tool inputs\n- Enables native human-in-the-loop patterns\n\n### 3. **Structured Output (Now Stable)**\n- Combine structured data generation with multi-step tool calling\n- Use `Output.object()`, `Output.array()`, `Output.choice()`, or `Output.text()`\n- Available in agents and `generateText`/`streamText` functions\n\n### 4. **Reranking Support**\n- Native support from Cohere, Amazon Bedrock, Together.ai\n- Improves search relevance by reordering documents based on query relationships\n- Supports both plain text and structured document reranking\n\n### 5. **Call Options**\n- Pass type-safe runtime inputs to dynamically configure agents\n- Use cases: RAG document injection, dynamic model selection, tool configuration per request\n\n## Migration from AI SDK 5.x\n\nThe documentation confirms that \"AI SDK 6 is expected to have minimal breaking changes\" and \"most AI SDK 5 code will work with little or no modification.\"\n\n### Timeline\n- **AI SDK 6 Beta:** Currently available\n- **Stable Release:** End of 2025\n\nFor detailed migration steps and API-specific changes, refer to the [migration guides](/docs/migration-guides) section of the documentation.",
