arbitrary JSON data\n   208→✅ Progress callbacks can track workflow execution (onProgress, onComplete, onError)\n   209→✅ The onProgress callback is called with status updates and accumulated text\n   210→✅ The onComplete callback is called with final results when workflow finishes\n   211→✅ The onError callback is called with error details when workflow fails\n   212→✅ Workflows emit AG-UI protocol events (RUN_STARTED, TEXT_MESSAGE_*, RUN_FINISHED, RUN_ERROR)\n   213→\n   214→### Workflow Tool Integration\n   215→\n   216→✅ Workflows can call back to client-side tools defined with defineTool\n   217→      ⚠️ **NOTE**: DifyWorkflowRunner does not implement tool callbacks yet.\n   218→✅ Tools can be provided to workflows via the trigger options\n   219→✅ Tool calls from workflows are tracked with names, arguments, and results\n   220→✅ The onProgress callback receives updated tool call information after each execution\n   221→✅ Tool execution errors are sent back to the workflow\n   222→\n   223→---\n   224→\n   225→## Protocol & Types\n   226→\n   227→### AG-UI Protocol\n   228→\n   229→✅ The AG-UI protocol defines standardized event types for AI-UI communication\n   230→✅ The protocol supports streaming text messages (TEXT_MESSAGE_START, _CONTENT, _END)\n   231→✅ The protocol supports streaming tool calls (TOOL_CALL_START, _ARGS, _END)\n   232→✅ The protocol supports run lifecycle events (RUN_STARTED, RUN_FINISHED, RUN_ERROR)\n   233→✅ The protocol supports state snapshots (STATE_SNAPSHOT, MESSAGES_SNAPSHOT)\n   234→🆗 The protocol supports thinking messages (THINKING_TEXT_MESSAGE_*, THINKING_START, THINKING_END)\n   235→   NOTE: Types are imported from @ag-ui/core but not implemented or tested in use-ai\n   236→🆗 The protocol supports chunked messages (TEXT_MESSAGE_CHUNK, TOOL_CALL_CHUNK)\n   237→   NOTE: Types are imported from @ag-ui/core; TEXT_MESSAGE_CHUNK tested, TOOL_CALL_CHUNK untested\n   238→🆗 The protocol supports activity tracking (ACTIVITY_SNAPSHOT, ACTIVITY_DELTA)\n   239→   NOTE: Types are imported from @ag-ui/core but not implemented or tested in use-ai\n   240→🆗 The protocol supports step tracking (STEP_STARTED, STEP_FINISHED)\n   241→   NOTE: Types are imported from @ag-ui/core but not implemented or tested in use-ai\n   242→🆗 The protocol supports raw and custom events (RAW, CUSTOM)\n   243→   NOTE: Types are imported from @ag-ui/core but not implemented or tested in use-ai\n   244→✅ All events support optional timestamps\n   245→\n   246→### Message Types\n   247→\n   248→✅ The protocol supports user, assistant, system, developer, and tool message roles\n   249→✅ Tool messages include tool call ID and result content\n   250→✅ Assistant messages can include tool calls\n   251→✅ The protocol supports activity messages for tracking activities\n   252→✅ The protocol supports binary content in messages (images, files, etc.)\n   253→\n   254→### Type Safety & Exports\n   255→\n   256→🆗 The client exports TypeScript types for all hooks, components, and configurations\n   257→🆗 The server exports TypeScript types for agents, plugins, and configurations\n   258→🆗 The core package exports AG-UI protocol types\n   259→🆗 Zod is re-exported from the client package for schema definitions\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n",
